00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.500
Which I appreciate that perspective,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.910
but I just want to remind you

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.680
that we talk about these
things for your entertainment.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.336
If you're not entertained,
there's many other options

00:03:07.336 --> 00:03:09.060
on the Internet.
Oh.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.673
Don't send a packing, man.

00:03:10.673 --> 00:03:12.114
Please don't go.

00:03:12.114 --> 00:03:13.164
Please don't go.

00:03:13.164 --> 00:03:13.997
Please like us.

00:03:13.997 --> 00:03:15.990
What I'm saying is we work very hard

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.580
for your entertainment,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.510
and also for the lifestyle
that we would like to live.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.950
And that involves doing things like

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.590
going and visiting your children
when they go off to college

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:28.320
or taking your wife on
a nice little trip away.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.600
We're not going to apologize
about those choices.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.440
And when we do them,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.120
we're gonna come back and
we're gonna talk about them

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.110
on this podcast.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:34.943
Oh, .

00:03:34.943 --> 00:03:37.260
You have the privilege
and the freedom to comment

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.160
about how you feel like we're
too privileged rich dudes

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.300
who complain about things,

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.130
because we are too privileged rich dudes

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.730
who do complain about things
for your entertainment.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.040
And we're going to continue to do that.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.830
We'll complain about
the things that bug us,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.050
and we'll celebrate the
things that please us,

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.630
and you're welcome to
come along for the ride.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.310
But we're gonna do what we wanna do.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.360
That's one take.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.920
I think the other take is I'm like,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.570
ooh, I'm cringing inside,

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:11.570
'cause I'm very self-conscious
about, okay, having money.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.470
It's a hang up of mine.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:17.700
I really-

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:18.987
I wasn't planning on talking about this,

00:04:18.987 --> 00:04:20.520
but you talked about how I look tired

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.650
and the reason I look tired is
because I'm a middle-aged man

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.620
who works his off running a company

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.453
and making entertainment.
And then you feel like

00:04:26.453 --> 00:04:28.650
you have to apologize for
complaining about your vacation

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.780
which you only did for
entertainment purposes.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:31.890
Right.
Right.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.270
I get that, I totally get it.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.223
I am not disagreeing.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:43.340
There is something about
the evolving relationship

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.830
that we have with Mythical
Beast, casual fans,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:54.720
I'm making a list now, just
interloping commenters,

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.230
and sometimes,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.330
so there's different categories of people

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.010
that we can get feedback from.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:06.180
Sometimes you don't know
how to weight that feedback.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.700
So on one hand, I don't wanna be like,

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.970
well, I don't listen to any feedback.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:12.930
And I'm not saying that.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.913
But like I was telling
you, I was listening to-

00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:16.920
I think we demonstrated that

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.350
we listened to quite a lot of feedback

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.183
and take that into account.

00:05:20.183 --> 00:05:22.110
If anything, a healthy exercise for us,

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.510
and I think this is maybe
what you're kind of embodying

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:29.510
at this point is that since
our tendency is to be so,

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.720
sensitive isn't the right word,

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.560
but there's a high fidelity
to the give and take

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.450
between us and the vocal Mythical Beast,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.830
the feedback that we get.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.900
It is very important, it's very valuable.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.250
If anything, we need to guard
against overweighting that

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.480
and not not going with our gut sometimes,

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.660
or not being ourselves or saying,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.490
I'm doing this for entertainment value

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.320
or I'm doing this to reach somebody,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.240
but it can be misunderstood

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.290
Yeah, I agree with that.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.090
I was just telling you that,

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.910
I don't really listen to Joe Rogan,

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.640
but Rick Rubin was a guest,

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:15.093
and I listen to everything
that Rick Rubin shows up on.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.660
That guy is so inspiring to me.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.250
So on the way in,

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.110
they were at a point in their conversation

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:27.110
where Rick was asking Rogan
about what kept him grounded

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:34.710
and what, despite
experiencing success and fame,

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.990
what keeps him sane.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.833
I think it was less of
grounded and more of sane,

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.420
'cause they were talking about,

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.420
there's a lot that goes along
with being in the public eye,

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.290
being successful, being
subject to so much scrutiny.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.580
And again, I'm not saying anything

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.580
about Joe Rogan's point of view
or stance on anything here,

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:03.590
but his response was he works out,

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.570
he does his cold plunge stuff,

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.580
which I know you're getting into that too.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.030
And so I thought this would
really resonate with you.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:12.863
And then he said,

00:07:12.863 --> 00:07:16.890
"I don't read what people say

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:20.640
or think about me at all, at all."

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.750
Yep.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.700
That's a privilege.

00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:25.770
That is a wild privilege.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.140
You can do that as a really
famous music producer.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:28.973
You cannot do that as an Internet person.

00:07:28.973 --> 00:07:31.530
Well, no, this was Joe Rogan
talking, not Rick Rubin.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:32.363
Oh, okay.

00:07:32.363 --> 00:07:35.010
So Joe doesn't listen to
what anybody says about him.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.060
And it shows.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.770
Yeah, and it shows.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.059
We're different people than him.

00:07:39.059 --> 00:07:39.892
So I think it would show-

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:41.130
We approach things in a different way,

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.800
But also if we didn't listen to anything,

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.950
I'd like to think we're
true enough to ourselves

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.450
and what we're putting out into the world,

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.420
that that's what Mythical
Beasts are connecting with

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.510
so that even if we didn't
listen to any feedback,

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:59.510
we would still be in this
safe zone of we're still us,

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.790
you're still you, we still
have this connection.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.380
But, and I actually don't
know what the but is.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.925
Well, I see, where you're going with this.

00:08:08.925 --> 00:08:10.920
I don't know my point is, so
you tell me where I'm going.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:15.540
I think that there is a
difference between accountability

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:19.350
and cowering in fear about being yourself.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.340
So for instance-

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.140
And I see that in myself sometimes.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.150
We have a big team and they
do read all the comments

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.220
and they know exactly
what people are saying.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.053
Good point.

00:08:27.053 --> 00:08:28.560
The team is listening and then telling us.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.757
So-
The team is listening.

00:08:29.757 --> 00:08:33.850
... recent example, we
did an episode of GMM

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.500
where it was our,

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.660
can we follow directions
in a different language?

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.830
And we decided we wanted to
feature American Sign Language

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.630
on that episode.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:49.200
And we had a deaf person
lined up to be the person

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.330
to do sign language, because again,

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.460
representation is important to us

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.800
and we were like we want
to get a deaf person

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.570
to actually do this.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.403
They, unfortunately-

00:08:58.403 --> 00:09:01.080
And our team, and by the
way, our team knew that.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.180
It's not something we needed to tell them.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.660
The GMM team already knew that

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.760
so that's what they were working on.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:08.593
Of course.

00:09:08.593 --> 00:09:10.110
It's not something we had to like,

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.580
well make sure you do it this way.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.413
Yeah, and so-

00:09:12.413 --> 00:09:14.730
They were going about it in
a way that I feel good about.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.850
That person was unable to make it.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.910
And of course our
production schedule is crazy

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.200
and very tight.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.200
And so Matt Carney's
friend was in town who,

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.210
you saw the guy who was on the episode

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:33.750
and his brother was deaf
and he had to learn,

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.130
the whole family had
to learn sign language

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.260
in order to communicate with the brother.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.210
So we were like, oh, that's a cool story.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.970
And it's not exactly what we wanted,

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.560
which was a deaf person,

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.400
but we made a decision
to still move forward

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.190
to be able to have ASL
featured on the show.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.710
And of course, we got immediate feedback

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:56.160
from a number of people about
how this was not inclusive

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.690
to the deaf community.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.040
And you know what?

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.040
We totally understand that and
we listen to that feedback,

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:08.550
and I think moving forward, it'll be like,

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.160
okay, even though we know the backstory,

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.010
which is we had somebody who
was ready to go who was deaf

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.320
and then we ended up
using a non deaf person

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.403
or a hearing person,

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.400
because that's a difficult thing

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.990
to explain and contextualize

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.160
and we did run the risk

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:26.220
of making the deaf
community feel excluded,

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:28.170
maybe we should have
taken a different tack.

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:29.250
And this is great feedback

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.840
and we'll taken it into
account moving forward.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:34.980
And we commented to the
people on Twitter who said it,

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.020
we commented on a TikTok video.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.130
That's accountability

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.050
and that is something that we listen to.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:45.050
But me being a person
of privilege and wealth

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.430
because of all the success
that we have garnered

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:49.050
for reasons that are a lot,

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.730
we're just very fortunate and very lucky

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.520
and right timing and
things have gone right,

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.073
and we do live an unusual lifestyle.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.250
but that is the life that we live.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.200
That is the life that we
have found ourselves in,

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:05.070
is being the CEOs of this
big company that's doing well

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.410
and having figured out this Internet game

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:10.020
and having the ability to
work really, really hard

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:10.853
all the time,

00:11:10.853 --> 00:11:12.600
but then take much needed breaks

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.100
and then come on this
podcast and talk about them.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.830
I understand that if you
are not in a situation

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.810
where you can afford a vacation

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:23.370
or you don't have a job that pays well,

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.740
you don't have a job that you even enjoy,

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.320
that it may be difficult to listen to us

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.210
to say that we do enjoy our job

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.320
and we do make a lot of money

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.150
and we do go on vacation.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.890
And again, what I'm saying is,

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:38.670
you have the right if
that's triggering for you

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.870
to not listen,

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.720
but I'm not going to
not talk about my life

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:46.200
because my life might
be triggering to you.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.430
And I just think that there's a place

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.930
where you have to draw the line.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.070
I wanna be sensitive to it

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:51.720
and I don't wanna make this podcast

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.390
all about two rich guys talking
about all the rich guy stuff

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.460
that they do, 'cause that would be stupid.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:57.293
But if you-

00:11:57.293 --> 00:11:59.160
And we don't do that, I don't think.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:02.730
But the podcast is about our lives.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:06.318
I mean that is it, this
is what you signed up for,

00:12:06.318 --> 00:12:07.151
this is what you click for.

00:12:07.151 --> 00:12:08.130
Yeah so this is us being ourselves,

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:11.163
