00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:28.800
This is crazy.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.290
And I'm like, yeah,
it's just, it's, I'm ...

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:33.930
And then I'm like, oh no, this can't,

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:36.963
I'm looking so forward to
this trip, I need this so bad.

00:23:38.460 --> 00:23:40.050
This can't happen.

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:42.600
So while they're rummaging
through the inside,

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.720
these two mechanics who
are stopping they're doing

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:49.080
to help us 'cause they know Christy

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:50.940
'cause we get so much work done there.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:52.710
It's good to have a mechanic you can trust

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:56.010
and they know your face if
not your name and your wallet.

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:59.577
So I was like, I can't, I can't do this.

00:24:00.833 --> 00:24:05.220
So then I just started wedging my fingers

00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:10.220
in between the door and
the fuselage of the car,

00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.713
and I'm like, something has to be done.

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:15.960
something has to-

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:17.130
You're prying at this point.

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:18.030
I'm prying.

00:24:18.030 --> 00:24:20.880
And then so I pull it hard
and then all of a sudden,

00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:22.410
pop.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:27.410
I just ripped the
outside of the body part,

00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:34.202
the smooth body part of the gas cap thing.

00:24:34.202 --> 00:24:36.690
I just ripped that whole sucker off.

00:24:36.690 --> 00:24:38.100
The door came off?

00:24:38.100 --> 00:24:39.510
The door came off in my hand.

00:24:39.510 --> 00:24:42.450
But it was just the facade of it.

00:24:42.450 --> 00:24:44.580
So then underneath,
there's this apparatus,

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.840
the thing that's actually broken

00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:47.280
that you have to push on.

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.113
And then at that point,

00:24:48.113 --> 00:24:53.060
they could take a flathead
screwdriver and pop that open.

00:24:53.970 --> 00:24:54.803
And then he said,

00:24:54.803 --> 00:24:56.976
"Well, because there's
a gas cap underneath it,

00:24:56.976 --> 00:24:59.730
don't push that thing all the way back in

00:24:59.730 --> 00:25:00.900
and you'll be fine.

00:25:00.900 --> 00:25:02.340
Just drive with this thing

00:25:02.340 --> 00:25:04.950
just kind of like flapping
open a little bit."

00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:07.560
So, but Christy and I both
had a similar thought.

00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:09.330
We were like, okay now we
can get back on the road,

00:25:09.330 --> 00:25:11.400
we can get gas, we went
back over and got gas

00:25:11.400 --> 00:25:14.250
and we're both independently
thinking the same thing.

00:25:14.250 --> 00:25:15.083
Which is strange

00:25:15.083 --> 00:25:16.620
'cause I don't like
thinking this type of stuff

00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:17.880
'cause I don't think I believe this way.

00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:21.780
But I was like, is this a
sign that we shouldn't go

00:25:21.780 --> 00:25:23.160
on this trip?

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:23.993
Wow, okay.

00:25:25.410 --> 00:25:27.780
It's like-
How did that come up?

00:25:27.780 --> 00:25:29.310
We talked about it a little bit later.

00:25:29.310 --> 00:25:33.343
Christy was like, "I kind of
feel well we shouldn't go."

00:25:33.343 --> 00:25:35.100
A bad omen.
A bad omen.

00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:37.410
I was like, nope, I'm
not believing in omens.

00:25:37.410 --> 00:25:38.280
This is not happening.

00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:40.593
I believe in going on
this trip, nothing else.

00:25:41.430 --> 00:25:43.500
But I got a little nervous.

00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:47.277
And then it is a six-hour
drive to Big Sur.

00:25:47.277 --> 00:25:51.510
And we stop for lunch,
we get back on the road,

00:25:51.510 --> 00:25:55.357
