00:26:23.580 --> 00:26:25.320
to then switch sides,

00:26:25.320 --> 00:26:28.380
the car just died completely.

00:26:28.380 --> 00:26:30.183
All the power just died.

00:26:31.620 --> 00:26:32.940
Car wouldn't crank.

00:26:32.940 --> 00:26:34.590
You didn't turn the car off, It just died.

00:26:34.590 --> 00:26:38.040
I didn't turn the car off, it knocked off.

00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:43.040
And I don't know, a 2018 Volkswagen Atlas,

00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:45.123
it's not supposed to knock off.

00:26:46.230 --> 00:26:51.230
And so here we are, we're on
the PCH, we're on highway one,

00:26:52.290 --> 00:26:54.180
just starting the scenic drive.

00:26:54.180 --> 00:26:55.013
Beautiful, beautiful.

00:26:55.013 --> 00:26:56.010
It's so beautiful.

00:26:56.010 --> 00:26:59.490
And we're sitting there,
I don't know what to do.

00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:04.490
I feel very inadequate.

00:27:04.680 --> 00:27:07.380
But then everything that
Christy's telling me

00:27:07.380 --> 00:27:08.910
doesn't make sense.

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:12.270
It's like, I feel like what
you're telling me right now,

00:27:12.270 --> 00:27:15.747
like, "Can you put it in park."

00:27:17.617 --> 00:27:19.117
"Try to use my key."

00:27:19.117 --> 00:27:20.250
"It doesn't see the key,

00:27:20.250 --> 00:27:22.200
it says that the battery's dead."

00:27:22.200 --> 00:27:23.550
Okay, I guess the battery's dead,

00:27:23.550 --> 00:27:25.170
but why of a sudden would you just stop

00:27:25.170 --> 00:27:26.730
on the side of the road and
the battery would be dead?

00:27:26.730 --> 00:27:29.553
And so we start fighting.

00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:31.863
Christy and I never,

00:27:32.970 --> 00:27:35.553
